# 4. Cart design

## 4.1 Basket rules

- One basket per restaurant.
- Adding from another restaurant creates a separate basket.
- Basket lines store item IDs, quantities, and option IDs, never trusted prices.
- Baskets can persist for 48 hours but are repriced whenever viewed.
- No order exists until confirmation.

## 4.2 After adding an item

Add the item and show one relevant optional suggestion at most once per order:

> Added 1× Chicken Shawarma. Want to add fries or a drink?

Buttons:

```text
Add fries
Add drink
No thanks
View basket
```

Do not repeatedly upsell after a decline or silence.

## 4.3 Basket card

The basket should show:

```text
Restaurant
Item lines and quantities
Option selections
Line totals
Subtotal
Delivery fee
Total in USD and LBP
Estimated preparation time
```

Buttons:

```text
Checkout
Add more
Edit basket
Clear basket
```

## 4.4 Editing natural language

Support:

```text
make it 3
remove the drink
change the burger to chicken
no onions
add two more
I changed my mind
```

The AI interprets the request, then calls deterministic basket tools.

After a change, show the updated summary. Do not silently apply an ambiguous change.

## 4.5 Multiple restaurants

Say clearly:

> This item is from **Restaurant B**, so it will be a separate order with its own delivery fee.

Keep each restaurant basket separate through checkout.

