# 6. Reordering and customer memory

## 6.1 Reorder entry points

Support:

```text
same order
usual
same as last time
نفس الطلب
زي العادة
el 3ade
reorder
```

A returning customer greeting may show:

```text
Reorder last order
See full menu
Try something different
```

## 6.2 Reorder behavior

A reorder is always a **new order**:

1. retrieve the previous non-cancelled/non-rejected order;
2. rebuild the cart from item IDs and option IDs;
3. reprice every line;
4. check availability;
5. check restaurant hours;
6. check delivery area;
7. check minimum order and COD cap;
8. show the new summary;
9. require confirmation.

If something changed:

> The garlic chicken is no longer available. I can remove it or suggest these two similar items.

## 6.3 Memory controls

Customers should be able to say:

```text
What do you remember about me?
Forget that I like spicy food
Remove my address
Delete my data
Stop personalized recommendations
```

Every durable preference should include:

```text
source
confidence
created_at
last_confirmed_at
expires_at
```

Never infer allergies, religion, medical status, or sensitive traits.

