# 7. Order lifecycle and restaurant operations

## 7.1 Recommended state machine

```text
pending
  → accepted
  → preparing
  → ready
  → out_for_delivery
  → delivered

pending → rejected
pending → cancelled
accepted → cancelled_by_restaurant
preparing → issue_requires_customer
out_for_delivery → delivery_failed
out_for_delivery → not_collected
```

Every transition must be:

- authorized;
- atomic;
- idempotent;
- logged with actor and timestamp;
- connected to customer and restaurant notifications.

## 7.2 Restaurant confirmation

Immediately after customer confirmation:

- create the order;
- send the customer receipt;
- send restaurant order card/dashboard alert;
- start the acceptance timer.

Restaurant actions:

```text
Accept
Reject
Call customer/support
```

If still pending after 90 seconds:

- notify the customer that confirmation is taking longer;
- alert Alo King operations;
- escalate once only;
- do not send duplicate alerts.

## 7.3 Kitchen timing

Avoid unnecessary messages. A recommended sequence is:

```text
Order received
Accepted + ETA
On the way + tracking
Delivered + rating
```

“Preparing” can be recorded without a separate customer notification unless it materially changes the ETA.

