# 9. Broadcast strategy

## 9.1 Broadcasts are campaigns, not blasts

Every paid campaign must have:

```text
objective
approved offer
eligible audience
consent proof
frequency check
template
budget
test batch
holdout group
attribution window
kill rules
```

## 9.2 Safe audience

At launch, use only:

- explicit marketing opt-in;
- prior order from the restaurant;
- no restaurant mute;
- no global opt-out;
- frequency cap passed;
- valid phone/WhatsApp state;
- delivery/service area still relevant.

## 9.3 Personalized broadcast content

The campaign defines the approved offer. The recommendation engine selects the best item or variant for each customer from verified menu data.

Example:

```text
Campaign objective: Reactivate customers inactive for 30+ days
Approved offer: Family meal for 4, $24
Customer history: ordered shawarma previously
Personalized suggestion: family shawarma meal
```

The AI may personalize wording but may not alter the offer price, eligibility, validity, or terms.

## 9.4 Campaign rollout

1. Internal test.
2. 10–25 customer test batch.
3. Observe delivery, read, replies, opt-outs, and fulfilment capacity.
4. Expand gradually.
5. Preserve holdout recipients.
6. Pause on quality or operational problems.

Recommended initial Alo King limits:

| Control | Rule |
|---|---:|
| Restaurant messages to one customer | Maximum 1 every 7 days |
| All restaurant promotions to one customer | Maximum 2 every 30 days |
| Quiet hours | 22:00–08:00 Asia/Beirut |
| New campaign test batch | 10–25 recipients |
| New restaurant daily campaign | 25–50 recipients |
| Portfolio quota target | Keep 30–50% headroom |

## 9.5 Broadcast opt-out

Support:

```text
STOP
UNSUBSCRIBE
إيقاف
إيقاف العروض
```

Use separate controls for:

- mute one restaurant;
- stop restaurant offers;
- global marketing opt-out.

Re-check consent immediately before each send.

