# 10. Loyalty and rewards program

## 10.1 Program goal

Loyalty should increase profitable repeat orders, not create uncontrolled discounts.

Use a wallet called **King Credits**, but keep it financially auditable.

## 10.2 Earning rules

Possible rewards:

| Action | Suggested reward |
|---|---:|
| Completed order | Fixed points or small credit based on net order value |
| Second order within 30 days | Bonus credit |
| Rating completion | Small non-cash reward, not required for positive rating |
| Successful referral | Reward only after first order is delivered |
| Off-peak order | Restaurant-funded or platform-funded bonus |
| Birthday/anniversary | Optional, with explicit date consent |

Avoid rewarding only positive ratings. Reward submitting honest feedback instead.

## 10.3 Redemption rules

- Credits apply only to eligible orders.
- Credits cannot exceed a configured percentage of the order subtotal.
- Credits cannot be applied to delivery fees unless explicitly funded.
- Credits expire only with clear notice.
- Refunds and cancellations reverse unearned credits.
- Every credit movement is an append-only ledger entry.

## 10.4 Ledger model

```text
loyalty_ledger
- id
- customer_id
- order_id or referral_id
- amount_usd
- amount_lbp_display
- type: earn | redeem | reverse | expire | manual_adjustment
- idempotency_key
- created_at
```

Never use only a mutable balance without a ledger.

## 10.5 Customer experience

Customer asks:

```text
credits
رصيدي
my rewards
```

Reply:

> You have **$3.50 King Credits** available. You can apply them to an eligible order.

Buttons:

```text
Apply to basket
How it works
History
```

