# Final recommended customer experience

The ideal interaction feels like this:

```text
Customer: “Marhaba, bade shi la 4 أشخاص الجمعة، مش حار.”

Alo King:
  Understands Lebanese Arabic + Arabic script.
  Knows the customer’s village.
  Filters out spicy items.
  Finds open restaurants delivering there Friday.
  Uses customer preferences and successful history.
  Shows three relevant family meals with prices.

Customer taps a meal.

Alo King:
  Shows customizations.
  Adds the selection to the restaurant basket.
  Suggests one relevant side once.
  Shows exact dual-currency basket.

Customer taps Checkout.

Alo King:
  Uses saved address and asks only for missing details.
  Reprices and validates availability.
  Shows final summary.

Customer taps Confirm order.

Alo King:
  Creates one idempotent order.
  Notifies the restaurant.
  Sends receipt and tracking link.
  Sends accepted/dispatch/delivery notifications.
  Requests honest feedback after delivery.
  Offers a measured loyalty reward.
  Later offers a relevant, consented restaurant campaign.
```

> **Alo King wins when ordering feels effortless, but the underlying system is extremely strict about truth, consent, money, state transitions, and exceptions.**
